== Roleplaying Background

The Old World is dying. From the north comes a tide of corruption that devours everything it touches. The Empire's borders have collapsed. The Dwarf Holds are silent. Even the Elves have abandoned their shores.

You are what remains. A warlord of a fractured realm, commanding the last loyal soldiers in a world that has forgotten hope. Your fortress is the only bastion of order for a hundred leagues. Every day brings new threats — not just from the armies of Chaos, but from within. Mutiny whispers among your own ranks. Resources dwindle. The gods have abandoned you.

But you did not come this far to die.

== Wave 2 Guide — The End Times

== Campaign Philosophy

Wave 2 introduces mechanics mods that fundamentally change how you play. Your approach must evolve:

- *Scarcity is the new normal.* Mechanics mods modify resource availability. Hoard nothing; everything flows.
- *Loyalty matters.* New loyalty systems mean your armies can fracture mid-campaign if mismanaged.
- *No safe zones.* Mechanics mods remove safe havens. Every province can be attacked by something new.

== Core Mechanics Changes

=== Loyalty System
Each army has a loyalty rating. Low-loyalty armies may defect, refuse orders, or mutiny.
- Keep army loyalty high through victories, gifts, and veteran retention.
- Avoid over-stretching — long marches reduce loyalty.

=== Resource Decay
Resources now decay over time if not managed actively.
- Build infrastructure to sustain resources.
- Capture resource nodes to prevent decay.

=== Faction Collapse
Factions that lose too many provinces crumble rapidly. AI factions will collapse faster, opening new fronts — and new opportunities.

== Difficulty Curve

Wave 2 is designed to be punishing. Key challenges:
- More aggressive AI opponents
- Reduced starting resources
- Random catastrophic events every few turns
- New enemy unit types added by mechanics mods

== Recommended Progression

- Turns 1-10: Consolidate your fortress. Secure initial resources. Build loyalty.
- Turns 11-25: Expand carefully. Take only provinces you can defend.
- Turns 26+: Begin offensive operations. Strike at weakened enemies.

== Prerequisites Before Wave 3

You should be comfortable with:
- Managing armies under the loyalty system
- Responding to resource scarcity
- Adapting to random catastrophic events
- Operating without safe zones or easy recovery